from pathlib import Path
from html import escape
report=Path('outputs/Stratus-1.1.0-visual-checks')
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Stratus 1.1.0 visual checks</title><style>body{font:16px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;margin:32px auto;padding:0 24px;max-width:1400px;background:#121a22;color:#e6edf2}h1,h2{line-height:1.25}p{max-width:1000px;color:#bdcbd7}a{color:#91d8ff}.grid,.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px}figure{margin:0}img{width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:8px}figcaption{margin:5px 0 22px;color:#bdcbd7}section{margin:38px 0}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{text-align:left;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #34424e}th{color:#91d8ff}@media(max-width:800px){.grid,.pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}td,th{padding:8px}}</style><h1>Stratus 1.1.0 · actual Minecraft visual checks</h1><p>16 October 2026. Minecraft 1.21.11 / Iris 1.10.8 / Sodium 0.8.14 / Apple M1 / Reference preset. <strong>Zero shader errors in the final run.</strong> Native offline compilation: 486 passes. Focused GPU probes: 13 cases, zero OpenGL errors. These are unretouched screenshots saved by Minecraft.</p><table><tr><th>Requested change</th><th>Delivered behavior</th></tr>'''
rows=[('AO to 1.0','Default and maximum 1.00, with a zero-AO comparison.'),('Consistent water','Shared tint, absorption and ripple field on tops, sides and underwater interfaces; overlapping faces composed once.'),('Physical clouds','Finite world-height volume at Y=192, thickness 40 blocks, with density below/inside/above and retained distant overcast sky.'),('Sky light leakage','Broad restrained daylight opening through thinner sky bands.'),('Subtle bloom','Two half-resolution bright-pixel blur passes; default strength 0.06, adjustable to zero.'),('Particles and thrown items','Forward HDR lighting; snowball, egg, ender pearl, real block-destruction fragments and smoke tested.'),('All outdoor blocks damp','Default block classification covers unlisted terrain, translucent blocks and block entities; skylight estimates outdoor exposure.'),('Remove damp noise','No random or world-position dampness field. GPU probes match at distant positions and across material/face classes.'),('Subtle face shading','Small diffuse brightness/tint changes from broad sky light and warm ground bounce. No new cast shadows.')]
for a,b in rows:html+=f'<tr><td>{escape(a)}</td><td>{escape(b)}</td></tr>'
html+='</table><section><h2>Water, blocks and particles</h2><div class="grid">'
items=[('overview','Ore dampness continuity and scene overview'),('materials','Full AO, uniform outdoor dampness and subtle face shading'),('water-sides','Falling water sides'),('water-top','Water top and side continuity'),('underwater','Deeper underwater attenuation'),('underwater-interface','Looking through the water interface'),('thrown-items','Moving ender pearl, egg and snowball'),('block-breaking-particles','Actual stone destruction fragments'),('smoke-particles','Smoke cutouts and transparency'),('rain-glass-slime','Rain, glass and translucent slime'),('bloom-night','Restrained lantern bloom at night'),('held-item','Held iron pickaxe with HUD visible')]
for name,label in items:
 file='release110-'+name+'.png';assert (report/file).exists()
 html+=f'<figure><a href="{file}"><img loading="lazy" src="{file}" alt="{escape(label)}"></a><figcaption>{escape(label)}</figcaption></figure>'
html+='</div></section><section><h2>Cloud layer and sky</h2><p>A thin overcast volume with soft shading, with the distant patterned sky above it. These views are from below, within and above the layer. It is a rendering approximation of cloud scattering.</p><div class="grid">'
for name,label in [('clouds-below','Below the finite cloud layer'),('clouds-inside','Within the cloud layer'),('clouds-above','Above the cloud layer'),('sky-light','Broad light opening in the sky')]:
 file='release110-'+name+'.png';html+=f'<figure><a href="{file}"><img loading="lazy" src="{file}" alt="{label}"></a><figcaption>{label}</figcaption></figure>'
html+='</div></section><section><h2>Effect controls compared</h2><p>These pairs use the final material and bloom functions. The sky was refined afterwards; the release scenes above were recaptured. Animated particles and lightmap flicker differ between frames. Vanilla texture grain remains; the procedural dampness noise has been removed.</p>'
for title,on,off in [('Dampness','materials-on','damp-off'),('Face shading','materials-on','face-off'),('AO strength','materials-on','ao-off'),('Bloom','bloom-on','bloom-off')]:
 html+=f'<h3>{title}</h3><div class="pair">'
 for name,label in [(on,'On'),(off,'Off')]:
  file='final110-'+name+'.png';html+=f'<figure><a href="{file}"><img loading="lazy" src="{file}" alt="{title} {label}"></a><figcaption>{label}</figcaption></figure>'
 html+='</div>'
html+='''</section><section><h2>VanillaTweaks version mismatch</h2><p>The supplied VanillaTweaks archive targets resource formats 84–97 (Minecraft 26.1–26.3), while Minecraft 1.21.11 uses format 75. Its black firefly model reproduced with shaders disabled. The separate compatibility pack selects the vanilla bush model and was enabled above VanillaTweaks for QA. A VanillaTweaks build for 1.21.11 is the preferred replacement.</p><a href="no-shaders-firefly.png"><img loading="lazy" src="no-shaders-firefly.png" alt="Black firefly model with shaders disabled"></a></section><p>No FPS benchmark or full normal-profile mod-stack test. Reference/Overworld visually checked; other presets and dimensions compiled offline only. Waterfall thickness, screen-space reflections and skylight exposure are approximations. <a href="results.json">Detailed results and screenshot hashes</a>.</p></html>'''
(report/'index.html').write_text(html)
print('Wrote review gallery with sixteen release screenshots and control comparisons')
